    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0626" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg546"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Russell to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1901.</hi></date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 610.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to herewith inclose a
                    copy, with translation, of the law passed by the Venezuelan Congress of 1882 in
                    regard to the entrance of foreign men-of-war into Venezuelan ports.</p>
                <p>This law was published in the Official Gazette of April 30 last, as the law in
                    force at present.</p>
                <p>The Belgian legation here had sent to the foreign office a copy of the late
                    Belgian regulations on this same subject, and the foreign minister in
                    acknowledging the communication of the Belgian chargé d’affaires sent a copy of
                    the inclosed decree as the law in force on the subject in Venezuela at
                    present.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William W.
                    Russell.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d507-a1.xml" xpointer="d507-a1"/>
